    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="18.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 18.1</head>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="18.1" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="262" ed="#robertson"/>Ki abat femme a terre pur fere lui force, la munte al seinur X sol.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="263" ed="#robertson"/>If anyone throws a woman to the ground in order to offer violence to her, the compensation to her lord for breach of his mund shall be 10 shillings.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="505"><ref target="clause:Af_11-1">Af 11.1</ref>; <ref target="clause:LeisWl_16">Leis Wl 16</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 11, 1 | (*s. o. 16)</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:LeisWl_16">Leis Wl 16</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 262–263 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text (K–M) not yet added</note>
